cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "zeta-audit: a verifier for Riemann zeta zero tables"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that audits a Riemann zeta zero table: row structure, |zeta(1/2+it)|
  residuals at sampled ordinates by two independent evaluators, an ordinate comparison
  against mpmath's own zero finder, and a windowed zero count taken from zeta itself that
  detects a missing ordinate. Demonstrated on Odlyzko's zeros1 (100,000 zeros) with a
  negative control that must fail.
authors:
  - family-names: "Imruobai"
    alias: "Imruobai"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KIDA-Nya/zeta-audit"
url: "https://github.com/KIDA-Nya/zeta-audit"
keywords:
  - riemann zeta
  - zeta zeros
  - zero table
  - verification
  - number theory
  - odlyzko
  - lmfdb
version: "0.4.1"
date-released: "2026-11-22"